From 9e5e11a52a7bb9dabfd732fc67b844fed6279416 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:36:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] ASoC: apple: t8140_aop_audio: J714c microphone setup of
 the T604x flow

On the firmware families where the host configures the PDM microphones
(aurora-silicon's aop_audio T604x flow, which follows macOS), the array's
start attaches pdm0, lpai and lilb, sets the lpai channel masks (property
300, three microphones), the PDM interface configuration (pdm0 property
200: pll clock, 2.4 MHz PDM, 24 MHz PDMC, 20 ms turn-on, 50 ms settle)
and the high-frequency decimator (pdm0 property 212, the T604x
coefficients), and requests pwrd with the parameter word 1. Payloads too
big for the stack are assembled on the heap. Each answer is reported and
a refusal does not stop the array. T8140 keeps its firmware's own setup.

J714c's firmware accepts every step (return 0) and the array still
records the idle noise floor only: the microphone input stays off.

[port to integration/aurora (aurora-j716s 6d9f1ec652a6): applied
 unchanged to sound/soc/apple/aop_t8140.rs, t8140_aop_audio.rs's name in
 this tree; DT and j714c.config hunks are board-specific and dropped]

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/apple/aop_t8140.rs | 318 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 315 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

